  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform circular disc of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> placed on a rough horizontal plane has initial velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> and angular velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;as shown. The disc comes to rest after moving some distance in the direction of motion. Then<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0066_b275154cff75.jpg\" style=\"width: 216px; height: 118px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The friction force acts in the forward direction",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The point of contact of disc with ground has zero velocity",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;must be equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;in magnitude",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;must be equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in magnitude",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Conserving the angular momentum of the disc about its bottom-most point, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;(Since the disc finally comes to rest, it means its total angular momentum is zero)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
